  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The Hybrid Practitioner (2022), published by Leuven University Press, has been cited 6 times. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 4,029 times and is used in teaching.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The Hybrid Practitioner by Caroline Voet, Eireen Schreurs Schreurs and Helen Thomas was published by Leuven University Press in 2022. Conceptually, the work connects to Appeal, Audience measurement, Engineering ethics, Publishing and Realm.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 6 citations. Citations peaked in 2026 with 5 citing works. Notable citing venues include International Journal of Architectural Research Archnet-IJAR and TECHNE - Journal of Technology for Architecture and Environment. They come from 4 countries, led by the United Kingdom, Sweden and Bulgaria.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">In teaching, it is discussed in 1 recorded lecture. It has been downloaded 4,029 times via OAPEN. Its subject matter aligns with Sustainable cities and communities among the Sustainable Development Goals. The work was funded by KU Leuven.</p>",
