  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The Hybrid Practitioner is showing an early but meaningful impact profile in architectural scholarship and teaching. It has 6 citations, 4,029 downloads, and one recorded teaching-related mention, suggesting that the book is being read, discussed, and used within practice-oriented architectural education.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Published by Leuven University Press in 2022, The Hybrid Practitioner argues for a closer relationship between architectural academia and design practice, and the impact record reflects that theme. The strongest signal is usage: the book has been downloaded 4,029 times through OAPEN, indicating sustained interest from readers rather than a purely symbolic presence in the literature.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Its citation record is still modest, with 6 citations in OpenAlex, but the citing literature is clearly aligned with the book\u2019s core concerns. Recent citations appear in architectural research journals and focus on design education, hybrid practice, knowledge production, pedagogy, and the relationship between university and professional work. That pattern suggests the book is being taken up as a reference point in conversations about how architectural knowledge is made and taught.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">There is also a signal of teaching adoption: the book is discussed in a recorded video associated with Henley Halebrown, which points to use beyond formal citation contexts. In addition, the book\u2019s alignment with Sustainable Cities and Communities indicates policy and sustainability relevance, especially given its focus on how architectural practice connects to material, social, and institutional settings.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, the record shows a book with clear resonance in architecture-related education and discourse, and with substantial reader uptake through open access distribution. The citation base is still developing, so the impact story is best read as emerging rather than mature, but the available evidence already shows reach across scholarly, pedagogical, and professional audiences.</p>",
